# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Reel Deal Deck — redirects
#
# Netlify-style; Cloudflare Pages reads the same format. First match wins, so
# order matters. `301!` forces the rule even when a file exists at that path.
#
# The single most valuable thing in this file is host canonicalisation. Every
# page carries <link rel="canonical"> pointing at https://reeldealdeck.com/…,
# so if www. or http:// also serve 200s you are splitting link equity between
# four addresses for the same page and confusing every crawler that finds one.
# Pick one host. It is the apex. Never change it after launch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Canonical host --------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify also does this automatically once reeldealdeck.com is set as the
# Primary domain in Domain management. These rules make it explicit and make
# the site portable to any other host.
http://reeldealdeck.com/*        https://reeldealdeck.com/:splat      301!
http://www.reeldealdeck.com/*    https://reeldealdeck.com/:splat      301!
https://www.reeldealdeck.com/*   https://reeldealdeck.com/:splat      301!

# --- Trailing-slash / index consistency ------------------------------------
# Every route this site emits is a directory with an index.html, so the
# canonical form always ends in "/". Netlify's Pretty URLs already 301s
# /deck -> /deck/ for any directory, including all 54 fly pages; these rules
# pin the nav routes explicitly so the behaviour does not depend on a toggle
# in a dashboard someone might switch off.
/index.html                      /                                    301!
/deck/index.html                 /deck/                               301!
/deck                            /deck/                               301
/flies                           /flies/                              301
/gifts                           /gifts/                              301
/wholesale                       /wholesale/                          301
/story                           /story/                              301
/conservation                    /conservation/                       301
/contact                         /contact/                            301

# --- Reserved alias --------------------------------------------------------
# Singular /fly/<slug>/ is the URL people guess and type, and the one a forum
# post is most likely to get wrong. Reserve it now; it costs nothing and it
# means no inbound link to the Fly Library can ever land on a 404.
/fly/*                           /flies/:splat                        301
/flys/*                          /flies/:splat                        301
/fly-library/*                   /flies/:splat                        301
/patterns/*                      /flies/:splat                        301

# --- Legacy / off-platform entry points ------------------------------------
# Add here as they appear. Examples of the shape they should take:
#   /kickstarter    https://www.kickstarter.com/…       302
#   /ig             https://instagram.com/reeldealdeck  302
# TODO-CONFIRM: the Kickstarter campaign URL, before adding a /kickstarter alias.

# --- Fallback --------------------------------------------------------------
# Not a wildcard SPA rewrite. dist/404.html (written by scripts/postbuild.mjs)
# is picked up by Netlify automatically and served with a real 404 status,
# which is what search engines need to see. Do not add `/* /index.html 200`.

